  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a chaotic street scene with burning tires and people in motion, suggesting unrest or conflict. The overlaid text reads: 'the media calls them refugees but this is what you will get.' This juxtaposition implies that refugees are inherently violent or dangerous, portraying them as a threat to society. The intent is to stoke fear and prejudice against refugees by associating them with destruction and disorder, which is a hateful stereotype. This aligns with Islamophobic tropes that link refugees or Muslim populations with terrorism and barbarism, and it also fits under harmful propaganda that seeks to dehumanize and incite hostility toward a vulnerable group.",
